Dafny now warns about a matching loop through a term with the variable of a nested quantifier, such as `F(i + j)` in `forall i :: F(i) <= 0 || forall j :: P(j) ==> F(i + j) > 1`, and says how to break it, here by replacing `i + j` with a new variable bound alongside `j`, as in `forall j, t | t == i + j`. Dafny used to introduce such a variable itself, in any nested quantifier, also where it did not break the loop.
